{%- comment -%}
  ═══ LBASS — MARKDOWN BADGE (card image) ═══

  The piece's OWN discount, stamped on the product image so the promotion is
  legible before a word is read.

  ── NOT THE CAMPAIGN RIBBON ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  snippets/lbass-promo-badge.liquid also puts a percentage on this image, and it
  means something completely different: «تخفيضات الصيف ‑30% على الثانية» is a
  discount on a SECOND item. This badge is how much THIS item is reduced.

  They are therefore deliberately NOT styled as one family:

      campaign ribbon   red     top-inline-START
      markdown badge    ink     top-inline-END

  A card can carry both. When it did — briefly, on 2026-09-09 — two red
  percentages sat one above the other meaning «this item is 25% off» and «a
  second item would be 30% off», and a shopper reading quickly takes the bigger
  number as this item's discount. The colour split is what keeps them apart, so
  do not "unify" it. The note in snippets/lbass-product-card.liquid records the
  same incident.

  Red is also already spoken for on this card: the 1/1 stamp, the percentage
  pill and the savings line are all red. A fourth red element is what makes a
  card look cheap.

  ── ARIA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  aria-hidden. The percentage and the saving are both announced properly by the
  price block a few elements later; a screen reader should not hear the discount
  three times.

  ── PARAMETERS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    product   required
    variant   optional — defaults to selected_or_first_available_variant
    pct       optional — precomputed percentage, as a string.
                         Pass it from a card that renders up to 250 times to
                         avoid a nested render per card; omit it anywhere else
                         and this file asks snippets/lbass-sale itself.

  USAGE
      {%- render 'lbass-markdown-badge', product: product -%}
      {%- render 'lbass-markdown-badge', product: product, pct: card_pct -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign lbm_pct = pct
  if lbm_pct == blank
    capture lbm_pct
      render 'lbass-sale', product: product, variant: variant
    endcapture
  endif
  assign lbm_pct = lbm_pct | strip
-%}
{%- if lbm_pct != '0' and lbm_pct != '' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    <bdi>, not dir="ltr" on the badge itself: direction on the box makes
    `inset-inline-end` resolve against the BADGE rather than the page, which
    pinned it to the right-hand corner in RTL too. bdi isolates the numeral run
    from the surrounding RTL text and leaves the box's logical axis alone.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="lb-md-badge" aria-hidden="true"><bdi dir="ltr">&minus;{{ lbm_pct }}%</bdi></span>
{%- endif -%}
